{"id":"bath-sheba-bathsheba","name":"Bath-Sheba (Bathsheba)","aliases":["Bath-Sheba"],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:bath-sheba-bathsheba"],"types":[],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Bath-sheba","text":"Daughter of the oath, or of seven, called also Bath-shu’a (1 Chr. 3:5), was the daughter of Eliam (2 Sam. 11:3) or Ammiel (1 Chr. 3:5), and wife of Uriah the Hittite. David committed adultery with her (2 Sam. 11:4, 5; Ps. 51:1). The child born in adultery died (2 Sam. 12:15-19). After her husband was slain (11:15) she was married to David (11:27), and became the mother of Solomon (12:24; 1 Kings 1:11; 2:13). She took a prominent part in securing the succession of Solomon to the throne (1 Kings 1:11, 16-21)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3678","lemma":"כִּסֵּא","xlit":"kiççêʼ","gloss":"covered","kjv":"seat, stool, throne","count":7,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H113","lemma":"אָדוֹן","xlit":"ʼâdôwn","gloss":"sovereign","kjv":"lord, master, owner","count":9,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H4428","lemma":"מֶלֶךְ","xlit":"melek","gloss":"a king","kjv":"king, royal","count":21,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","xlit":"mâlak","gloss":"to reign","kjv":"consult, indeed, be  king, be  queen","count":7,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H7812","lemma":"שָׁחָה","xlit":"shâchâh","gloss":"to depress","kjv":"bow  down, crouch, fall down, humbly beseech","count":4,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H7650","lemma":"שָׁבַע","xlit":"shâbaʻ","gloss":"to seven oneself","kjv":"adjure, charge, feed to the full ), take an oath","count":4,"share":0.11}],"verses":["1Kgs.1.13","1Kgs.1.17","1Kgs.1.20","1Kgs.1.24","1Kgs.1.27","1Kgs.1.30","1Kgs.2.19","2Sam.11.2","2Sam.11.3","2Sam.11.4","2Sam.11.5","1Kgs.1.11","1Kgs.1.12","1Kgs.1.14","1Kgs.1.15","1Kgs.1.16","1Kgs.1.18","1Kgs.1.19","1Kgs.1.21","1Kgs.1.22","1Kgs.1.23","1Kgs.1.25","1Kgs.1.26","1Kgs.1.28","1Kgs.1.29","1Kgs.1.31","1Kgs.2.13","1Kgs.2.14","1Kgs.2.15","1Kgs.2.16","1Kgs.2.17